# STATION 2: per-NPC memory, player-wide memory, once-blocks, visited(), guarded starts.
# Two NPCs share this file. Talk to A first, then B.
npc: @test_memory
title: Station 2 - Memory
speaker: Tester

start: returning when $met
start: first

== first
TEST 2: Memory. This is our FIRST meeting. Expected: NPC B will also say "first meeting" even after you finish here, because $met is per NPC.
<<set $met = true>>
<<set $player.visits = $player.visits + 1>>
<<once>>
  This once-block line should appear exactly once per NPC, ever.
<<endonce>>
<<jump menu>>

== returning
TEST 2: Memory. Welcome BACK. Expected: you only see this after finishing a first meeting with THIS NPC.
<<jump menu>>

== menu
Player-wide counter: you have opened this station's dialogue {$player.visits} time(s) across both NPCs.
-> Check visited(): have I seen the "elsewhere" node? (expect no the first time, yes after visiting it)
    <<if visited("elsewhere")>>
      Yes, you have visited "elsewhere" with this NPC.
    <<else>>
      Not yet. Pick the "Visit elsewhere" option, then ask again.
    <<endif>>
-> Visit elsewhere
    <<jump elsewhere>>
-> Reset my memory of this NPC (sets $met back to false; next open should be a first meeting again)
    <<set $met = false>>
    Done. Leave and talk to me again.
-> Leave
    <<end>>

== elsewhere
You are in "elsewhere". visited("elsewhere") is now true for this NPC.
-> Back
    <<jump menu>>
